---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, COMPANY_EMAIL } from "../links";
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="whereti makes no network connections, and this website sets no cookies and loads nothing from elsewhere. The details." prose>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    whereti never connects to the internet, and this website keeps no record of you. Below is exactly what that means.
  </p>
  <p class="updated">Last changed on 25 October 2026.</p>

  <h2 id="app">The app</h2>
  <p>
    None of the programs whereti installs makes a network request: not the search window, not the background service,
    not the document reader, not the installer. There is no account, no telemetry, no crash reporting and no update
    check that phones home. To get a new version, you download it from this site or from GitHub yourself.
  </p>
  <p>What whereti keeps, all on your PC:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The index</strong> of file names and document words, in <code>%ProgramData%\whereti</code>. Windows lets
      only itself and administrators read it, because it lists every file on the PC.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your settings</strong> (language, theme, shortcut, folders to skip) in
      <code>%AppData%\whereti\settings.txt</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    whereti keeps no history of what you search. The recent files it shows before you type come from Windows' own list
    of recent files. Uninstalling whereti removes the index and the settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking pixels, no ads.</li>
    <li>Nothing is loaded from another site: the font, the icons and the images are served from whereti.com.</li>
    <li>The server keeps no access log, so ordinary visits leave no IP address behind.</li>
    <li>
      The theme you pick (light or dark) is remembered in your own browser, not sent to us. Choosing the theme of your
      system forgets it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Downloads come from GitHub, which sees the request like any download. GitHub's own privacy statement applies to it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="email">If you write to us</h2>
  <p>
    E-mails are read by the people who make whereti and kept only as long as the conversation needs. They are not shared
    or used for anything else.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights, formally</h2>
  <p>
    The controller is Software Hive S.R.L., CUI RO54366095, Voicești, Vâlcea, Romania
    (<a href={`mailto:${COMPANY_EMAIL}`}>{COMPANY_EMAIL}</a>). Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, have it
    corrected or deleted, and object to how it is used. In practice we hold nothing unless you have e-mailed us. You can
    also complain to the Romanian data protection authority,
    <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ro">ANSPDCP</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>
</Base>
